# correction-words.local — what counts as the user correcting the AI.
#
# Read by tools/session-digest.sh, which feeds harness/hooks/suggest-retro.sh: a
# session with corrections in it is a session that probably taught something.
#
# One extended-regex alternative per line. Blank lines and #-comments are ignored.
# If this file exists it REPLACES the built-in English defaults entirely — so if you
# add a second language, re-list the English terms you still want.
#
# Keep it conservative. A false positive costs one wasted question; a nudge that fires
# on every session is a nudge that gets switched off.
#
# Example, for someone who works in two languages (English and German shown):
#
# ^(no|nope|nein|not quite|wrong|falsch)\b
# \b(actually|instead|revert|undo|misread|incorrect|not what i|rather than)\b
# \b(eigentlich|stattdessen|lieber|nicht so|doch nicht)\b
